# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AWS CDK deployment stack — deliberately unpublished
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The stack fronts the app with a public ALB (publicLoadBalancer: true) but sets
# neither TYPECAST_AUTH_MODE nor TYPECAST_NO_AUTOLOGIN. Both default to local
# mode, so app/api/deps.py returns the local user for every request and anyone
# who finds the ALB hostname reads and writes the manuscripts. SECRET_KEY is also
# a hardcoded literal, which would be public along with the rest of the source,
# making tokens forgeable and the stored AI keys decryptable.
#
# Publish this only after: TYPECAST_AUTH_MODE=multi, SECRET_KEY injected from
# Secrets Manager, and the internet-facing listener documented.
deploy/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User data — never commit a manuscript or its media
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
backend/uploads/
uploads/
content/
codex/
